IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Carbon Pricing Act 2018 (Singapore) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- A fact here is one a witness or a record could give ("the plant burned
-- 40,000 tonnes of natural gas in 2025"); whether that makes the plant a
-- taxable facility is a rule.
--
-- Source: ../source/CPA2018.txt (SSO PDF, current version as at 06 Oct 2026).

§ `Carbon Pricing Act 2018 — the nouns`

§§ `Greenhouse gas emissions`

-- Second Schedule Parts 2 and 3, second column: the circumstances in which a
-- gas is emitted that the Act distinguishes. Anything else is `in any other
-- circumstances`.
DECLARE `Circumstance of emission` IS ONE OF
    `in manufacturing, installing, using or disposing of electrical equipment`     -- Part 2 item 2 (SF6)
    `used and emitted in purging`                                                   -- item 3(a) (CO2)
    `used and emitted in blasting`                                                  -- item 3(b) (CO2)
    `in using any lubricant or paraffin wax`                                        -- item 3(c) (CO2)
    `in the combustion of a biomass fuel listed in item 3(d)`                       -- item 3(d) (CO2)
    `in using refrigeration or air-conditioning equipment for non-manufacturing purposes` -- items 4, 5 (HFCs, PFCs)
    `in using any fire protection equipment`                                        -- item 6(a)
    `as a fugitive emission, not flaring or venting`                                -- item 6(b)
    `in using a vehicle to transport persons or goods`                              -- item 6(c); Part 3 item 1(a)
    `in using a fuel on which excise duty is payable or exempt under the Customs Act 1960` -- item 6(d)
    `in carrying out AFOLU activities`                                              -- item 6(e); Part 3 item 1(b)
    `in any other circumstances`

-- One gas emitted directly from a business facility (s 2 "GHG emission"), its
-- mass in metric tonnes, and how it was emitted. The gas is named as in the
-- First Schedule's first column ("Carbon dioxide", "HFC-134a", "PFC-14").
DECLARE `GHG emission` HAS
    `gas`            IS A STRING
    `mass in tonnes` IS A NUMBER
    `circumstance`   IS A `Circumstance of emission`

§§ `Business facilities and operational control (ss 3, 4)`

-- s 3: a business facility is a single site at which a business activity is
-- carried out; s 4: operational control. Whether a set of activities is one
-- facility, and who has operational control, is a finding the caller makes
-- (with s 3(3)-(4) and s 4(3)); these facts let the rules check the site test.
DECLARE `Site facts` HAS
    `carried out on more than one parcel of land`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the same person has operational control over the activity`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(3)
    `parcels contiguous, adjacent, adjoining, or separated only by a road, pathway, drain or waterway` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(3)(a)
    `a prescribed dependency between the activities on the parcels`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(3)(b)
    `in a prescribed industry sector`                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(1)

DECLARE `Policy authority` HAS
    `person`                                     IS A STRING
    `may introduce and implement operating policies`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(1)(a)
    `may introduce and implement health and safety policies` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(1)(b)
    `may introduce and implement environmental policies`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4(1)(c)
    `rank of authority`                          IS A NUMBER    -- s 4(3): higher is greater authority; a finding

§§ `Registration (Part 3)`

-- What the person (and the facility) already are, on the register.
DECLARE `Registration status` HAS
    `a registered person`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a reportable facility of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a taxable facility of the person`    IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(5), s 8(1)(a)(ii): a transfer of operational control from X to Y.
DECLARE `Transfer of control` HAS
    `date of transfer`                                         IS A DATE
    `X was a registered person of the facility, or had control on 31 December of a trigger year` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(5)(a)
    `the facility was registered as a taxable facility of X`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 8(1)(a)(ii)(B)-(C)
    `reckonable tCO2e in the year before the transfer`         IS A NUMBER    -- s 8(1)(a)(ii)(A)-(B)

-- s 9: grounds to deregister.
DECLARE `Deregistration facts` HAS
    `ceased to have operational control`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(1)(a), (3)(a)
    `ceased to operate with no intention to resume within 36 months` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (aa)
    `reckonable tCO2e in each of the last 3 consecutive years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER   -- (b)
    `a modification was completed`                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `reckonable tCO2e in the year the modification was completed` IS A NUMBER  -- (c)(i)
    `likely tCO2e in each of the next 2 years`                  IS A LIST OF NUMBER   -- (c)(ii): the Agency's or the person's forecast
    `no reportable facility remains registered to the person`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(4)
    `wound up, dissolved or otherwise ceased to exist`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(5)
    `all obligations and liabilities under the Act discharged`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10(4)

§§ `Tax, assessments and payment (Part 5)`

DECLARE `Kind of assessment` IS ONE OF
    `an assessment under s 21(1)`            -- on approving the verified report(s)
    `a best-judgment assessment under s 21(2)`
    `an advance assessment under s 22`
    `a revised assessment under s 23`

-- How the tax for one emissions year was, or is to be, paid.
DECLARE `Payment record` HAS
    `tax assessed`                              IS A NUMBER
    `assessment`                                IS A `Kind of assessment`
    `notice of assessment served on`            IS A DATE
    `amount paid by the due date`               IS A NUMBER
    `amount still unpaid on the as-at date`     IS A NUMBER

-- Fixed-price and international carbon credits offered in payment.
DECLARE `Surrender` HAS
    `fixed-price carbon credits`                IS A NUMBER
    `eligible international carbon credits`     IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed ICC limit`                  IS A NUMBER     -- s 33B(1); regulations
    `the Minister permits more ICCs`            IS A BOOLEAN    -- s 33B(2)
    `ICCs may be used for that tax and emissions year` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 17(3A): prescribed

DECLARE `FPCC account state` IS ONE OF
    `open`
    `suspended`
    `closed`

§§ `Appeals and decisions (Part 6)`

DECLARE `Agency decision` IS ONE OF
    `refusing to deregister a taxable facility`                         -- s 34(1)(a)
    `refusing to approve a verified emissions report or monitoring plan` -- (b)
    `refusing a refund or a credit of FPCCs under s 19`                  -- (c)
    `refusing to revise an assessment under s 23`                        -- (d)
    `some other decision`

§§ `Offences`

DECLARE `CPA offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 47(2) — refusing or misstating name, address or particulars`
    `s 48(3) — failing to comply with a requirement on search`
    `s 49(4) — failing to comply with a notice to provide information`
    `s 51(2) — failing to carry out a test or inspection`
    `s 52 — obstructing the Agency or an authorised officer`
    `s 53 — false entries or false information`
    `s 54(1) — failing to apply to be a registered person`
    `s 54(2) — failing to apply to register a reportable facility`
    `s 54(3) — failing to apply to register a taxable facility`
    `s 54(4) — false statement in a registration application`
    `s 54(5) — failing to give 45 days' notice of ceasing control`
    `s 55(1) — failing to submit an unverified emissions report`
    `s 55(2) — submitting an inaccurate unverified emissions report`
    `s 56(1) — failing to submit a verified emissions report`
    `s 57(1) — failing to submit a monitoring plan`
    `s 57(2) — submitting an inaccurate monitoring plan`
    `s 58 — failing to comply with a direction under s 13(2), 14 or 15(2), or with s 15(1)`
    `s 60 — offences by authorised and unauthorised persons`
    `s 61(1) — failing to comply with the Minister's requirement`
    `s 61(2) — failing to attend before an Appeal Panel`
    `s 62(1) — failing to keep records`
    `s 62(2) — failing to notify a change in particulars`
    `s 70(3) — failing to comply with a court's remedial order`
    `s 76(4) — contravening the regulations`

-- s 56(2)-(5): the culpability behind an inaccurate verified report.
DECLARE `Culpability` IS ONE OF
    `none shown`                                                   -- s 56(2)
    `without reasonable excuse or through negligence`              -- (3)
    `wilfully with intent to evade`                                -- (4)
    `by fraud, art or contrivance, wilfully with intent to evade` -- (5)

-- What a court may impose, at most. A NUMBER of dollars; imprisonment in
-- months; a daily amount for a continuing offence after conviction.
DECLARE `CPA penalty` HAS
    `fine`                       IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment in months`     IS A NUMBER
    `continuing, per day`        IS A NUMBER
